Z||000000||JetroGT||06-04-2001||04:21 PM||||And I spent almost a grand!<BR>It's crazy. Nobody around sells re-man control arms except the Fiero store. I bought upper and lower arms, ultimate dog bone and a rear GT decklid weather strip. Don't get me wrong, I am greatful that they had the parts that I needed. But man that money goes quick.||||reg||14
Z||000001||JetroGT||06-08-2001||07:34 AM||||I just got everything I ordered. I put the weather stripping on the trunk and I installed the dog bone. I can actually tell the difference with the new dog bone. On start up I can feel the vibrations through the seat. And it seems to shift alot firmer with less shudder. Tuesday I get the control arms put on. I hope it's done and ready before the Alamo area Fiero show, since I missed the Dells Run.||||reg||14
Z||000002||FieroJoe||06-08-2001||10:37 AM||||I liked the dogbone I got from them for my 4cly.  It dosent vibrate that much more than my rubber one.  It does feel much tigher though, but I still need to check out my lower motor mounts, they may be crapped out too.<P>The FieroStore has some great customer service, never had a problem with them and they ship quickly.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||06-08-2001||11:13 AM||||I agree, the money adds up fast. Especially on their web site. I spent $2200 in about 1/2 hour.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DecadenceR||06-08-2001||12:08 PM||||In the past 2 weeks I ordered from them 3 times.<BR>They're great with returns too. You just call up, tell them what you wanna return, and they give you the number and you send it!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||06-08-2001||05:31 PM||||Did you tell them you belong to a Fiero club and get your 10% off? <BR>The Fiero Store will give you 10% off if you belong to a Fiero club. But they only take the discount on aftermarket parts. Any Original GM parts cannot be discounted.||||reg||12
